> Module Form_w2s
> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Form W-2: wages, withholding, Medicare and social security checks

Catala module for Direct File `formW2s.xml` (issue #12, `scope.md` section
3.2). It computes what the rest of the return reads from the filer's Forms
W-2: Form 1040 line 1a (wages), line 25a (federal income tax withheld), the
social security and Medicare tax withheld used by Schedule 8812, Form 8880
line 2 deferrals, nontaxable combat pay (code Q), employer HSA contributions
(code W) and the knockout conditions that send W-2 shapes Direct File does
not support out of scope.

Conventions: `catala/CONVENTIONS.md`. Every dollar amount a W-2 carries is an
`input` here (complete inputs, section 3 of the conventions: an empty box is an
explicit `$0`). A Direct File `Round` is `R.round_dollar` and is applied
exactly where the XML applies it (per-item rounding, section 4, rule 2).

Oracle: `oracle/facts.csv` rows `/wages`, `/formW2Withholding`,
`/socialSecurityTaxesWithheld`, `/allCombatPay`, `/combatPayAmount`, compared
by `make difftest SCOPE=form_w2s` (mapping `difftest/mappings/form_w2s.mjs`).

## Facts skipped

Not modelled, because they are MeF export helpers, screen-flow state or state
tax inputs (conventions section 2, last rows; the state-return facts are out of
scope in issue #12):

- Every `...Needed` fact (for example `/formW2s/*/457bDeferralsNeeded`,
  `combatPayNeeded`) and every `...Rounded` fact whose only reader is the MeF
  export. The `...Rounded` facts that feed a tax figure (Form 8880 line 2, code
  W) are reproduced as inline `R.round_dollar` calls.
- Identity and address facts: `tin`, `usedTin`, `flowFilerTinIsSsn`, `ein`,
  `employerName`, `writableEmployerNameLine2`, `employerAddress`, `suffix`,
  `addressMatchesReturn`, `addressOverride`, `address`.
- Screen state and validation: `hasSeenLastAvailableScreen`, `isComplete`,
  `formW2sIsDone`, `primaryFilerHasIncompleteFormW2s`,
  `secondaryFilerHasIncompleteFormW2s`, `hasW2ValidationErrors`,
  `hasInputBox12Codes`, `writableHasBox12Codes`, `hasBox12Codes`,
  `writableBox12Code`, `nonstandardOrCorrectedChoice`, `isCorrected`,
  `isNonstandard`, `standardOrNonStandardCd`, `w2NonstandardCorrectedOptions`,
  `oneAndOnlyW2`, `filersHaveExactlyOneW2` (read only by the CDCC provider
  screens), `xmlHasW2s`, `hasW2s` (only decides whether MeF attaches W-2
  records), `w2MinAmount`, `formW2WithAllocatedTips`, `formW2WithBox12Knockout`,
  `formW2sWithBox12KnockoutCodes`.
- Box 7 social security tips (`writableOasdiTips`, `oasdiTips`): no tax figure
  in scope reads it.
- Box 13 `retirementPlan`: no tax figure reads it.
- Box 14 and boxes 15 to 20 (state and local): `box14*`, `BOX14_*`,
  `hasRRTACodesInBox14`, `flowKnockoutHasRRTACodesInBox14NotInNY`,
  `hasABox14NYRRTAValueWeKnockout`, `knockoutBox14NYRRTACode`, the
  `414H`/`ERS`/`NYSERS`/... code facts, `state`, `stateWages`,
  `stateWithholding`, `localWages`, `localWithholding`, `locality`,
  `flowKnockoutBox15IncomeFromDifferentState`, `knockoutYonkersPartYear`,
  `partYearYonkersResident`, `flowStateToolNeedsBox14`, `hasStateWagesWithoutStateCode`,
  `box17GreaterThanBox16`, `box19GreaterThanBox18`. These belong to the state
  knockout issues (#36, #37).
- `hasQsehra`: read only by `ptc.xml` and left to the PTC issues (#32 to #34).
  The raw box 12 amount `qsehra_benefits` (code FF) is an input field so they
  can read it.
- Imported W-2 variants (`imported*`, `isImported`): `imported.xml` is not
  modelled (conventions section 9).

## Shapes

```catala-metadata
# The "Form W-2 box 12 code" options of `/w2Box12CodeOptions` are the
# `code_...` fields of `FormW2` below. A Catala identifier cannot start with a
# digit, so DF names such as `401kDeferrals` become `deferrals_401k`
# (`403bDeferrals` -> `deferrals_403b`, `457bDeferrals` -> `deferrals_457b`,
# `501c18Deferrals` -> `deferrals_501c18`, `409aDeferrals` -> `deferrals_409a`,
# `83iIncome` -> `income_83i`, `83iDeferrals` -> `deferrals_83i`,
# `457bIsGovernmentalPlan` -> `plan_457b_is_governmental`).

## One Form W-2 as the filer typed it.
## DF: the `/formW2s` collection. Every box is a `writable...` fact in DF.
declaration structure FormW2:
  # DF: /formW2s/*/filer
  data filer content Types.FilerRole
  # Box 1. DF: /formW2s/*/writableWages
  data writable_wages content money
  # Box 2. DF: /formW2s/*/writableFederalWithholding
  data writable_federal_withholding content money
  # Box 3. DF: /formW2s/*/writableOasdiWages
  data writable_oasdi_wages content money
  # Box 4. DF: /formW2s/*/writableOasdiWithholding
  data writable_oasdi_withholding content money
  # Box 5. DF: /formW2s/*/writableMedicareWages
  data writable_medicare_wages content money
  # Box 6. DF: /formW2s/*/writableMedicareWithholding
  data writable_medicare_withholding content money
  # Box 8. DF: /formW2s/*/writableAllocatedTips
  data writable_allocated_tips content money
  # Box 10. DF: /formW2s/*/writableDependentCareBenefits
  data writable_dependent_care_benefits content money
  # Box 11. DF: /formW2s/*/writableNonQualifiedPlans
  data writable_non_qualified_plans content money
  # Box 12, one field per code.
  # A. DF: uncollectedOasdiTaxOnTips
  data uncollected_oasdi_tax_on_tips content money
  # B. DF: uncollectedMedicareTaxOnTips
  data uncollected_medicare_tax_on_tips content money
  # C. DF: taxableLifeInsuranceOver50k
  data taxable_life_insurance_over_50k content money
  # D. DF: 401kDeferrals
  data deferrals_401k content money
  # E. DF: 403bDeferrals
  data deferrals_403b content money
  # F. DF: sarsepDeferrals
  data sarsep_deferrals content money
  # G. DF: 457bDeferrals
  data deferrals_457b content money
  # H. DF: 501c18Deferrals
  data deferrals_501c18 content money
  # J. DF: nontaxableSickPay
  data nontaxable_sick_pay content money
  # K. DF: goldenParachuteExciseTax
  data golden_parachute_excise_tax content money
  # L. DF: expenseReimbursements
  data expense_reimbursements content money
  # M. DF: uncollectedOasdiTaxOnLifeInsuranceOver50k
  data uncollected_oasdi_tax_on_life_insurance_over_50k content money
  # N. DF: uncollectedMedicareTaxOnLifeInsuranceOver50k
  data uncollected_medicare_tax_on_life_insurance_over_50k content money
  # P. DF: armedForcesMovingExpenses
  data armed_forces_moving_expenses content money
  # Q. DF: writableCombatPay
  data writable_combat_pay content money
  # R. DF: archerMsaContributions
  data archer_msa_contributions content money
  # S. DF: simpleContributions
  data simple_contributions content money
  # T. DF: adoptionBenefits
  data adoption_benefits content money
  # V. DF: nsoIncome
  data nso_income content money
  # W. DF: employerHsaContributions
  data employer_hsa_contributions content money
  # Y. DF: 409aDeferrals
  data deferrals_409a content money
  # Z. DF: nqdcDeferrals
  data nqdc_deferrals content money
  # AA. DF: roth401kContributions
  data roth401k_contributions content money
  # BB. DF: roth403bContributions
  data roth403b_contributions content money
  # DD. DF: healthCoverageCost
  data health_coverage_cost content money
  # EE. DF: roth457bContributions
  data roth457b_contributions content money
  # FF. DF: qsehraBenefits
  data qsehra_benefits content money
  # GG. DF: 83iIncome
  data income_83i content money
  # HH. DF: 83iDeferrals
  data deferrals_83i content money
  # II. DF: nonTaxableMedicaidWaiverPayments
  data non_taxable_medicaid_waiver_payments content money
  # Answer to "is this a governmental 457(b) plan?", asked only when code G is
  # present. DF: /formW2s/*/457bIsGovernmentalPlan
  data plan_457b_is_governmental content boolean
  # Box 13. DF: /formW2s/*/statutoryEmployee
  data statutory_employee content boolean
  # Box 13. DF: /formW2s/*/thirdPartySickPay
  data third_party_sick_pay content boolean

## How the filer elects to treat nontaxable combat pay (Form 1040 line 1i and
## the earned income credit). DF: `/combatPayElection` (`eitc.xml`) with the
## options of `/combatPayOptions` (`constants.xml` lines 837 to 880). The
## options DF offers depend on who has combat pay; this module accepts any
## value and applies the same six cases as `/combatPayAmount`.
declaration enumeration CombatPayElection:
  -- NoCombatPay
  -- UsePrimaryCombatPay
  -- UseSpouseCombatPay
  -- UseBothCombatPay
  -- UsePrimaryNotSpouseCombatPay
  -- UseSpouseNotPrimaryCombatPay
```

## Per-item facts (`/formW2s/*/...`)

Form 1040 line 1a: "Total amount from Form(s) W-2, box 1"
(`sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf` p 1). Instructions, "Line 1a",
`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 23: "Enter the total amount
from Form(s) W-2, box 1. If a joint return, also include your spouse's income
from Form(s) W-2, box 1."

Instructions for line 25a (`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 37): "Add the amounts shown as
federal income tax withheld on your Form(s) W-2. Enter the total on line 25a.
The amount withheld should be shown in box 2 of Form W-2."

The scope `FormW2Item` below computes the derived facts of one W-2. The
collection scope `FormW2s` maps it over the list.

```catala-metadata
## The derived facts of a single Form W-2 and the checks that read it.
declaration scope FormW2Item:
  input w2 content FormW2
  # Echo of `w2.filer`, so a list of results can be filtered by filer.
  output filer content Types.FilerRole
  # DF: /formW2s/*/wages (box 1, rounded)
  output wages content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/federalWithholding (box 2, rounded)
  output federal_withholding content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/oasdiWages (box 3, rounded)
  output oasdi_wages content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/oasdiWagesForKnockoutCalculation
  output oasdi_wages_for_knockout_calculation content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/oasdiWithholding (box 4, rounded)
  output oasdi_withholding content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/medicareWages (box 5, rounded)
  output medicare_wages content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/medicareWithholding (box 6, rounded)
  output medicare_withholding content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/allocatedTips (box 8, rounded)
  output allocated_tips content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/dependentCareBenefits (box 10, not rounded)
  output dependent_care_benefits content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/nonQualifiedPlans (box 11, rounded)
  output non_qualified_plans content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/combatPay (box 12 code Q, rounded)
  output combat_pay content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/employerHsaContributionsRounded (box 12 code W)
  output employer_hsa_contributions_rounded content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/totalDeferralsAndContributions (Form 8880 line 2)
  output total_deferrals_and_contributions content money
  # DF: /formW2s/*/causesAllocatedTipsKO
  output causes_allocated_tips_ko condition
  # DF: /formW2s/*/causesNonQualifiedPlansKO
  output causes_non_qualified_plans_ko condition
  # DF: /formW2s/*/hasBox12KnockoutCode (via /formW2s/*/knockoutBox12Code)
  output has_box12_knockout_code condition
```

### Box amounts

DF rounds each dollar box on its own (`Round` around the `Switch`), so a W-2
with $30,000.40 in box 1 reports $30,000. `writableDependentCareBenefits` is
the one box DF does not round per item (`/formW2s/*/dependentCareBenefits`
has no `Round`); the sum over the filer's W-2s is rounded instead
(`/primaryFilerDependentCareBenefits`).

```catala
scope FormW2Item:
  definition filer equals w2.filer

  # QUIRK(Q-R1): per-item rounding. Form 1040 instructions p 23 say to add the
  # cents and round the total; DF rounds each W-2 first. Decision: reproduce
  # (CONVENTIONS section 4 rule 2, issue #60).
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/wages
  definition wages equals R.round_dollar of w2.writable_wages
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/federalWithholding
  definition federal_withholding equals
    R.round_dollar of w2.writable_federal_withholding
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/oasdiWages
  definition oasdi_wages equals R.round_dollar of w2.writable_oasdi_wages
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/oasdiWithholding
  definition oasdi_withholding equals
    R.round_dollar of w2.writable_oasdi_withholding
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/medicareWages
  definition medicare_wages equals R.round_dollar of w2.writable_medicare_wages
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/medicareWithholding
  definition medicare_withholding equals
    R.round_dollar of w2.writable_medicare_withholding
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/allocatedTips
  definition allocated_tips equals R.round_dollar of w2.writable_allocated_tips
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/dependentCareBenefits (no Round)
  definition dependent_care_benefits equals w2.writable_dependent_care_benefits
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/nonQualifiedPlans
  definition non_qualified_plans equals
    R.round_dollar of w2.writable_non_qualified_plans
  # Box 12 code Q. DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/combatPay
  definition combat_pay equals R.round_dollar of w2.writable_combat_pay
  # Box 12 code W. DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/employerHsaContributionsRounded
  definition employer_hsa_contributions_rounded equals
    R.round_dollar of w2.employer_hsa_contributions
```

### Social security wage base across W-2s

Pub. 15 (2024), `sources/pubs/p15--2024.pdf` p 2: "The social security wage
base limit is $168,600." A filer with several employers can have more than that
withheld, and is then owed a refund of the excess (Schedule 3 line 11,
"Excess social security and tier 1 RRTA tax withheld",
`sources/forms-instructions/f1040s3--2024.pdf` p 1), which Direct File does not
support (`ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages` below). To avoid knocking out a
filer with many W-2s that each have small social security wages, DF counts at
most the wage base from each W-2.

```catala
scope FormW2Item:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/oasdiWagesForKnockoutCalculation
  # (LesserOf of oasdiWages and /maxOasdiWagesOnMultipleW2sForOnePerson)
  definition oasdi_wages_for_knockout_calculation equals
    Money.min of oasdi_wages, P.oasdi_wage_base
```

### Form 8880 line 2: deferrals and contributions

Form 8880 line 2, `sources/forms-instructions/f8880--2024.pdf` p 1:
"Elective deferrals to a 401(k) or other qualified employer plan, voluntary
employee contributions, and 501(c)(18)(D) plan contributions for 2024 (see
instructions)". The instructions (same file, p 2) say "Include on line 2 any of
the following amounts. Elective deferrals (including designated Roth
contributions under section 402A, if applicable) to a 401(k), 403(b),
governmental 457(b), SEP, SIMPLE, or to the federal TSP. Voluntary employee
contributions to a qualified retirement plan, as defined in section 4974(c)
(including the federal TSP). Contributions to a 501(c)(18)(D) plan. These
amounts may be shown in box 12 of your Form(s) W-2 for 2024."

Direct File adds up these box 12 codes, each rounded on its own: D (401(k)),
E (403(b)), F (SARSEP), G (457(b), only when the plan is governmental),
H (501(c)(18)(D)), S (SIMPLE), AA (Roth 401(k)), BB (Roth 403(b)), EE (Roth
457(b)). The 457(b) test is the answer to "is this a governmental plan?", which
is what separates code G amounts that count (governmental 457(b)) from those
that do not (a tax-exempt organization's 457(b) is not an eligible plan for the
credit).

```catala
scope FormW2Item:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/totalDeferralsAndContributions, a sum of the
  # /formW2s/*/normalizedRounded...Deferrals/Contributions facts; with complete
  # inputs each of those is the rounded box 12 amount.
  definition total_deferrals_and_contributions equals
    (R.round_dollar of w2.deferrals_401k)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.deferrals_403b)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.sarsep_deferrals)
    # Only include code G if it is a governmental 457(b) plan.
    + (if w2.plan_457b_is_governmental
       then R.round_dollar of w2.deferrals_457b
       else $0)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.deferrals_501c18)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.simple_contributions)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.roth401k_contributions)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.roth403b_contributions)
    + (R.round_dollar of w2.roth457b_contributions)
```

### Knockouts on one W-2

Direct File stops at W-2 shapes it cannot compute. Each condition is an
`output` and is gathered into `FormW2s.unsupported` below
(conventions section 6).

Box 8, allocated tips. 1040 instructions, "Tip Income Not Reported on Line 1a"
(`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 23): "This should include any tip income you didn't
report to your employer and any allocated tips shown in box 8 on your Form(s)
W-2 unless you can prove that your unreported tips are less than the amount in
box 8." That needs Form 4137, which is not supported.

Box 11, nonqualified plans: distributions from a nonqualified deferred
compensation plan are taxed through the pension lines; DF does not support
them.

Box 12: DF knocks out the filer when any of codes A, B, F, J, K, L, M, N, P,
R, T, Z or II has a value above zero. Note the test uses the unrounded box
amount: `$0.40` is above zero. Codes C, D, E, G, H, Q, S, V, W, Y, AA, BB, DD,
EE, FF, GG and HH never knock out. The list is the `Switch` in
`/formW2s/*/knockoutBox12Code` (`formW2s.xml` lines 2807 to 3093).

```catala
scope FormW2Item:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/causesAllocatedTipsKO
  rule causes_allocated_tips_ko under condition allocated_tips > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/causesNonQualifiedPlansKO
  rule causes_non_qualified_plans_ko under condition non_qualified_plans > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2s/*/hasBox12KnockoutCode, which is IsComplete of
  # /formW2s/*/knockoutBox12Code; that Switch is complete exactly when one of
  # the 13 listed codes is above $0.
  rule has_box12_knockout_code under condition
    w2.uncollected_oasdi_tax_on_tips > $0                              # A
    or w2.uncollected_medicare_tax_on_tips > $0                        # B
    or w2.sarsep_deferrals > $0                                        # F
    or w2.nontaxable_sick_pay > $0                                     # J
    or w2.golden_parachute_excise_tax > $0                             # K
    or w2.expense_reimbursements > $0                                  # L
    or w2.uncollected_oasdi_tax_on_life_insurance_over_50k > $0        # M
    or w2.uncollected_medicare_tax_on_life_insurance_over_50k > $0     # N
    or w2.armed_forces_moving_expenses > $0                            # P
    or w2.archer_msa_contributions > $0                                # R
    or w2.adoption_benefits > $0                                       # T
    or w2.nqdc_deferrals > $0                                          # Z
    or w2.non_taxable_medicaid_waiver_payments > $0                    # II
  consequence fulfilled
```

## All Forms W-2 of the return

```catala-metadata
## The Forms W-2 of the return and everything derived from the whole list.
declaration scope FormW2s:
  ## DF: /formW2s
  input w2s content list of FormW2
  ## DF: /filingStatus
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  ## DF: /filers/<primary>/canBeClaimed
  input primary_filer_can_be_claimed condition
  ## DF: /filers/<secondary>/canBeClaimed. Ignored when there is no secondary
  ## filer.
  input secondary_filer_can_be_claimed condition
  ## DF: /combatPayElection (`eitc.xml`)
  input combat_pay_election content CombatPayElection

  internal items content list of FormW2Item
  internal primary_items content list of FormW2Item
  internal secondary_items content list of FormW2Item
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFJ
  internal is_filing_status_mfj condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFS
  internal is_filing_status_mfs condition

  # Form 1040 lines 1a and 25a
  # DF: /wages
  output wages content money
  # DF: /formW2Withholding
  output form_w2_withholding content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityTaxesWithheld
  output social_security_taxes_withheld content money

  # Per filer wages (earned income for CDCC, elderly or disabled credit)
  # DF: /primaryFilerWages
  output primary_filer_wages content money
  # DF: /secondaryFilerWages
  output secondary_filer_wages content money
  # DF: /primaryFilerHasW2WagesGreaterThan0
  output primary_filer_has_w2_wages_greater_than_0 condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerHasW2WagesGreaterThan0
  output secondary_filer_has_w2_wages_greater_than_0 condition

  # Dependent care benefits (box 10), for Form 2441
  # DF: /primaryFilerDependentCareBenefits
  output primary_filer_dependent_care_benefits content money
  # DF: /secondaryFilerDependentCareBenefits
  output secondary_filer_dependent_care_benefits content money

  # Form 8880 line 2 (before the Saver's credit eligibility filter and rounding
  # that `saversCredits.xml` applies)
  # DF: sum of /primaryFilerW2s/*/totalDeferralsAndContributions
  output primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions content money
  # DF: sum of /secondaryFilerW2s/*/totalDeferralsAndContributions
  output secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions content money

  # HSA, box 12 code W
  # DF: /primaryFilerTotalHsaContributionsFromW2s
  output primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s content money
  # DF: /secondaryFilerTotalHsaContributionsFromW2s
  output secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s content money
  # DF: /hasPrimaryFilerHsaContributionsFromW2s
  output has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s condition
  # DF: /hasSecondaryFilerHsaContributionsFromW2s
  output has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s condition
  # DF: /totalHsaContributionsOnW2s
  output total_hsa_contributions_on_w2s content money
  # DF: /hasHsaContributionsOnW2
  output has_hsa_contributions_on_w2 condition

  # Nontaxable combat pay, box 12 code Q
  # DF: /primaryFilerCombatPay
  output primary_filer_combat_pay content money
  # DF: /MFJSpouseCombatPay
  output mfj_spouse_combat_pay content money
  # DF: /primaryFilerHasCombatPay
  output primary_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /MFJSpouseHasCombatPay
  output mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /someFilerHasCombatPay
  output some_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /onlyOneFilerHasCombatPay
  output only_one_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /onlyPrimaryFilerHasCombatPay
  output only_primary_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /onlyMFJSpouseHasCombatPay
  output only_mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /bothFilersHasCombatPay
  output both_filers_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: /bothFilersCombatPay
  output both_filers_combat_pay content money
  # Form 1040 line 1i. DF: /combatPayAmount
  output combat_pay_amount content money
  # Schedule 8812 line 18b. DF: /allCombatPay
  output all_combat_pay content money

  # Medicare wages
  # DF: /formW2totalMedicareWages
  output form_w2_total_medicare_wages content money
  # DF: /primaryFilerMedicareWages
  output primary_filer_medicare_wages content money
  # DF: /secondaryFilerMedicareWages
  output secondary_filer_medicare_wages content money
  # DF: /maxMedicareWagesForAnyFilerOnReturn
  output max_medicare_wages_for_any_filer_on_return content money
  # DF: /medicareWagesAdditionalTaxThreshhold
  output medicare_wages_additional_tax_threshold content money
  # DF: /anyFilerExceedsEligibleForMedicareWagesCredit
  output any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit condition
  # DF: /anyFilerRequiredToPayExtraMedicareTax
  output any_filer_required_to_pay_extra_medicare_tax condition

  # Social security wages across W-2s of one filer
  # DF: /primaryFilerW2sCount
  output primary_filer_w2s_count content integer
  # DF: /secondaryFilerW2sCount
  output secondary_filer_w2s_count content integer
  # DF: /primaryFilerTotalOasdiWagesForKnockout
  output primary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout content money
  # DF: /secondaryFilerTotalOasdiWagesForKnockout
  output secondary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout content money
  # DF: /primaryFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages
  output primary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages
  output secondary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages condition

  # Knockouts, conventions section 6
  # DF: /flowKnockoutAllocatedTips
  output ko_flow_knockout_allocated_tips condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutStatutoryEmployee
  output ko_flow_knockout_statutory_employee condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutThirdPartySickPay
  output ko_flow_knockout_third_party_sick_pay condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutNonQualifiedPlans
  output ko_flow_knockout_non_qualified_plans condition
  # DF: /knockoutForBox12Value
  output ko_knockout_for_box12_value condition
  # DF: /knockoutForBox12Dependency
  output ko_knockout_for_box12_dependency condition
  # DF: /knockoutMedicareWages
  output ko_knockout_medicare_wages condition
  # DF: /anyFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages
  output ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages condition
  output unsupported condition
```

### Setup

`/primaryFilerW2s` and `/secondaryFilerW2s` are filters of `/formW2s` by the
`filer` reference (`/formW2s/*/belongsToPrimaryFiler`,
`/formW2s/*/belongsToSecondaryFiler`).

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  definition items equals
    map each w among w2s to (output of FormW2Item with { -- w2: w })
  definition primary_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.filer = Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
  definition secondary_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.filer = Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition is_filing_status_mfj equals
    filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition is_filing_status_mfs equals
    filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
```

### Form 1040 lines 1a and 25a and the Schedule 8812 social security taxes

DF sums the already rounded items and rounds the sum again (a no-op on whole
dollars, kept so the definition mirrors the XML): `/wages`,
`/formW2Withholding`.

`/socialSecurityTaxesWithheld` is "the amount of social security and medicare
tax withheld, as defined by §24(d)(2)". 26 U.S.C. § 24(d)(2)(A)
(`sources/statute/irc-24.html`): "The term "social security taxes" means, with
respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year (i) the amount of the taxes
imposed by sections 3101 and 3201(a) on amounts received by the taxpayer during
the calendar year in which the taxable year begins". Section 3101 is the
employee's share of social security (box 4) and Medicare (box 6). Section
24(d)(2)(B) excludes taxes for which the taxpayer is entitled to a special
refund under section 6413(c) (the excess over the wage base), a case DF turns
into a knockout instead (`ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages`).

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  # Form 1040 line 1a, f1040--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: formW2s.xml /wages
  definition wages equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.wages))
  # Form 1040 line 25a, f1040--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2Withholding
  definition form_w2_withholding equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.federal_withholding))
  # IRC 24(d)(2)(A)(i). DF: formW2s.xml /socialSecurityTaxesWithheld
  definition social_security_taxes_withheld equals
    R.round_dollar of
      ((Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.oasdi_withholding))
       + (Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.medicare_withholding)))
```

### Per-filer wages, dependent care benefits, deferrals and HSA

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerWages
  definition primary_filer_wages equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among primary_items to x.wages)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerWages
  definition secondary_filer_wages equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among secondary_items to x.wages)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerHasW2WagesGreaterThan0
  rule primary_filer_has_w2_wages_greater_than_0 under condition
    primary_filer_wages > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerHasW2WagesGreaterThan0
  rule secondary_filer_has_w2_wages_greater_than_0 under condition
    secondary_filer_wages > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerDependentCareBenefits (Round of the sum)
  definition primary_filer_dependent_care_benefits equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of (map each x among primary_items to x.dependent_care_benefits))
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerDependentCareBenefits (Round of the sum)
  definition secondary_filer_dependent_care_benefits equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of
        (map each x among secondary_items to x.dependent_care_benefits))

  # Form 8880 line 2a (you) and 2b (your spouse).
  # DF: saversCredits.xml /unfilteredPrimaryFilersDeferralsAndContributions
  # rounds this sum; every item is already whole dollars, so the sum is too.
  definition primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among primary_items to x.total_deferrals_and_contributions)
  definition secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among secondary_items to x.total_deferrals_and_contributions)

  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerTotalHsaContributionsFromW2s
  definition primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among primary_items to
        (R.round_dollar of x.employer_hsa_contributions_rounded))
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerTotalHsaContributionsFromW2s
  definition secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among secondary_items to x.employer_hsa_contributions_rounded)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /hasPrimaryFilerHsaContributionsFromW2s
  rule has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s under condition
    primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /hasSecondaryFilerHsaContributionsFromW2s
  rule has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s under condition
    secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /totalHsaContributionsOnW2s (the spouse counts only if MFJ)
  definition total_hsa_contributions_on_w2s equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
         + secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
    else primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
  # DF: formW2s.xml /hasHsaContributionsOnW2
  rule has_hsa_contributions_on_w2 under condition
    total_hsa_contributions_on_w2s > $0
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Nontaxable combat pay

1040 instructions, "Nontaxable Combat Pay" (`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 25 to 26):
the filer may elect to include nontaxable combat pay in earned income for the
earned income credit and the credit for child and dependent care expenses, and
reports the elected amount on line 1i. Code Q of box 12 reports it. On a joint
return each spouse decides separately, so the combat pay is kept per filer.

`/combatPayAmount` picks the amounts by `/combatPayElection`. No election (or
"noCombatPay") gives `$0`. An election for a spouse who has no combat pay is
not one of the options DF offers (`/combatPayOptions`), and falls to `$0`
here as it does in the XML.

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerCombatPay
  definition primary_filer_combat_pay equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among primary_items to x.combat_pay)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /MFJSpouseCombatPay (zero unless MFJ)
  definition mfj_spouse_combat_pay equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then Money.sum of (map each x among secondary_items to x.combat_pay)
    else $0
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerHasCombatPay
  rule primary_filer_has_combat_pay under condition primary_filer_combat_pay > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /MFJSpouseHasCombatPay
  rule mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay under condition mfj_spouse_combat_pay > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /someFilerHasCombatPay
  rule some_filer_has_combat_pay under condition
    mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay or primary_filer_has_combat_pay
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /onlyOneFilerHasCombatPay
  rule only_one_filer_has_combat_pay under condition
    ((not is_filing_status_mfj) and primary_filer_has_combat_pay)
    or (is_filing_status_mfj and mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay
        and (not primary_filer_has_combat_pay))
    or (is_filing_status_mfj and (not mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay)
        and primary_filer_has_combat_pay)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /onlyPrimaryFilerHasCombatPay
  rule only_primary_filer_has_combat_pay under condition
    primary_filer_has_combat_pay and (not mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /onlyMFJSpouseHasCombatPay
  rule only_mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay under condition
    mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay and (not primary_filer_has_combat_pay)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /bothFilersHasCombatPay
  rule both_filers_has_combat_pay under condition
    mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay and primary_filer_has_combat_pay
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /bothFilersCombatPay
  definition both_filers_combat_pay equals
    primary_filer_combat_pay + mfj_spouse_combat_pay

  # Form 1040 line 1i. DF: formW2s.xml /combatPayAmount (Round of a Switch of
  # six cases; the default case is $0).
  definition combat_pay_amount equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if only_primary_filer_has_combat_pay
          and combat_pay_election = UsePrimaryCombatPay
       then primary_filer_combat_pay
       else if only_mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay
          and combat_pay_election = UseSpouseCombatPay
       then mfj_spouse_combat_pay
       else if both_filers_has_combat_pay
          and combat_pay_election = UseBothCombatPay
       then mfj_spouse_combat_pay + primary_filer_combat_pay
       else if both_filers_has_combat_pay
          and combat_pay_election = UsePrimaryNotSpouseCombatPay
       then primary_filer_combat_pay
       else if both_filers_has_combat_pay
          and combat_pay_election = UseSpouseNotPrimaryCombatPay
       then mfj_spouse_combat_pay
       else $0)

  # Schedule 8812 line 18b: all nontaxable combat pay of every W-2, whoever the
  # filer is. DF: formW2s.xml /allCombatPay
  definition all_combat_pay equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.combat_pay))
```

### Medicare wages and Form 8959

Form 8959 (Additional Medicare Tax), Part I (`sources/forms-instructions/f8959--2024.pdf`
p 1): "1 Medicare wages and tips from Form W-2, box 5. If you have more than one
Form W-2, enter the total of the amounts from box 5. ... 5 Enter the following
amount for your filing status: Married filing jointly $250,000; Married filing
separately $125,000; Single, Head of household, or Qualifying surviving spouse
$200,000. 6 Subtract line 5 from line 4. ... 7 Additional Medicare Tax on
Medicare wages. Multiply line 6 by 0.9% (0.009)."

Direct File does not compute Form 8959. It knocks the filer out as soon as the
Form 8959 threshold for the filing status is passed
(`/knockoutMedicareWages`). In a joint return a spouse with more than $200,000
of Medicare wages is also a knockout, even if the couple's total is below
$250,000: that spouse owes Additional Medicare Tax withholding at the employer
level (`/anyFilerExceedsEligibleForMedicareWagesCredit`).

Both comparisons are strict ("greater than"), so exactly the threshold is not
a knockout.

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2totalMedicareWages
  definition form_w2_total_medicare_wages equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.medicare_wages)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerMedicareWages
  definition primary_filer_medicare_wages equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among primary_items to x.medicare_wages)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerMedicareWages
  definition secondary_filer_medicare_wages equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among secondary_items to x.medicare_wages)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /maxMedicareWagesForAnyFilerOnReturn (GreaterOf)
  definition max_medicare_wages_for_any_filer_on_return equals
    Money.max of primary_filer_medicare_wages, secondary_filer_medicare_wages

  # Form 8959 line 5. DF: formW2s.xml /medicareWagesAdditionalTaxThreshhold
  definition medicare_wages_additional_tax_threshold equals
    if is_filing_status_mfs then P.additional_medicare_tax_threshold_married_separate
    else if is_filing_status_mfj then P.additional_medicare_tax_threshold_joint
    else P.additional_medicare_tax_threshold_other

  # DF: formW2s.xml /anyFilerExceedsEligibleForMedicareWagesCredit
  rule any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit under condition
    is_filing_status_mfj
    and (primary_filer_medicare_wages > P.medicare_wages_individual_limit
         or secondary_filer_medicare_wages > P.medicare_wages_individual_limit)
  consequence fulfilled

  # Form 8959 would be required. DF: formW2s.xml /knockoutMedicareWages
  rule ko_knockout_medicare_wages under condition
    any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit
    or form_w2_total_medicare_wages > medicare_wages_additional_tax_threshold
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: formW2s.xml /anyFilerRequiredToPayExtraMedicareTax. With complete
  # inputs, the `Not(IsComplete) or Not(...)` second operand reduces to the
  # negation of the credit test.
  rule any_filer_required_to_pay_extra_medicare_tax under condition
    ko_knockout_medicare_wages
    and (not any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit)
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Social security wage base across W-2s

Several employers each withhold social security tax on the first $168,600 of
pay (`P.oasdi_wage_base`, Pub. 15 p 2). A filer with more than one W-2 whose
combined social security wages pass the wage base may have had too much
withheld, and claims the excess on Schedule 3 line 11. DF does not support
that. The test is per filer (a spouse's W-2s do not count against the
primary filer) and needs at least two W-2s for that filer.

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerW2sCount
  definition primary_filer_w2s_count equals number of primary_items
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerW2sCount
  definition secondary_filer_w2s_count equals number of secondary_items
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerTotalOasdiWagesForKnockout
  definition primary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among primary_items to x.oasdi_wages_for_knockout_calculation)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerTotalOasdiWagesForKnockout
  definition secondary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among secondary_items to x.oasdi_wages_for_knockout_calculation)
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages
  rule primary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages under condition
    primary_filer_w2s_count > 1
    and primary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout > P.oasdi_wage_base
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages
  rule secondary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages under condition
    secondary_filer_w2s_count > 1
    and secondary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout > P.oasdi_wage_base
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /anyFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages
  rule ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages under condition
    primary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
    or secondary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Other knockouts

Box 13 statutory employee and third-party sick pay: both need forms DF does
not provide (Schedule C for a statutory employee; third-party sick pay
changes who owes the payroll tax). Box 12 code W with a filer who can be
claimed as a dependent: an HSA contribution on a dependent's W-2 is not
supported.

```catala
scope FormW2s:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /flowKnockoutAllocatedTips
  rule ko_flow_knockout_allocated_tips under condition
    exists x among items such that x.causes_allocated_tips_ko
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /flowKnockoutStatutoryEmployee
  rule ko_flow_knockout_statutory_employee under condition
    exists w among w2s such that w.statutory_employee
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /flowKnockoutThirdPartySickPay
  rule ko_flow_knockout_third_party_sick_pay under condition
    exists w among w2s such that w.third_party_sick_pay
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /flowKnockoutNonQualifiedPlans
  rule ko_flow_knockout_non_qualified_plans under condition
    exists x among items such that x.causes_non_qualified_plans_ko
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /knockoutForBox12Value
  rule ko_knockout_for_box12_value under condition
    exists x among items such that x.has_box12_knockout_code
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: formW2s.xml /knockoutForBox12Dependency, via
  # /formW2s/*/hasBox12HsaContributionsAndDependent: the W-2's filer can be
  # claimed, and code W is present and above $0 (rounded).
  rule ko_knockout_for_box12_dependency under condition
    exists x among items such that
      x.employer_hsa_contributions_rounded > $0
      and ((x.filer = Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler and primary_filer_can_be_claimed)
           or (x.filer = Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler and secondary_filer_can_be_claimed))
  consequence fulfilled

  # One place that lists every knockout of this module (conventions section 6).
  # The `flow.xml` entries are knockoutForBox12Value, knockoutForBox12Dependency,
  # flowKnockoutAllocatedTips, flowKnockoutStatutoryEmployee,
  # flowKnockoutThirdPartySickPay, flowKnockoutNonQualifiedPlans,
  # knockoutMedicareWages, anyFilerExceedsMaxOasdiWages. The state-related
  # entries of `flow.xml` (box 15, box 14 New York RRTA, Yonkers) are not part
  # of this module.
  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_knockout_for_box12_value
    or ko_knockout_for_box12_dependency
    or ko_flow_knockout_allocated_tips
    or ko_flow_knockout_statutory_employee
    or ko_flow_knockout_third_party_sick_pay
    or ko_flow_knockout_non_qualified_plans
    or ko_knockout_medicare_wages
    or ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  consequence fulfilled
```
